From 868158b36d03fdb56200c9bd370051bca9f21769 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Barth <dbarth4@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 13:44:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Make the tracing subscriber optional, behind `rust.logging`

`rustc_log` links `tracing-subscriber` (with `EnvFilter`) and `tracing-tree`
into every rustc, because `init_rustc_env_logger` runs at startup. For a
compiler nobody is going to run under `RUSTC_LOG` that is dead weight.

Put the gate in `rustc_log` itself rather than in `rustc_driver_impl`. A new
`subscriber` feature, on by default, carries `tracing-subscriber` and
`tracing-tree`; without it `init_logger` becomes a stub that warns when a
filter was actually requested. Everything else the crate offers stays:
`LoggerConfig`, `Error`, and the `tracing` / `tracing_core` re-exports that
rustdoc, miri, the error index generator and the cranelift and gcc backends
compile against. So none of those tools need a change, and `extern crate
rustc_log` keeps resolving in the sysroot either way.

Gating in `rustc_driver_impl` instead does not work: with `rustc_log` out of
the graph it is not built at all, and tools that name it fail with E0463.
Putting it back as a standalone sysroot rlib fails at link time too, because
the sysroot only carries `.rmeta` for third-party crates, not `.rlib`.

`rustc_driver_impl::init_logger_with_additional_layer` is the one item that
must be cfg'd out: its bound names `rustc_log::BuildSubscriberRet`, which is
defined in terms of `tracing_subscriber`. Its only in-tree caller is miri,
behind miri's own non-default `tracing` feature.

The `logging` feature is on by default at each link of the chain
(`rustc-main` -> `rustc_driver` -> `rustc_driver_impl` -> `rustc_log`), so an
unconfigured cargo build is unchanged. Bootstrap gains `rust.logging`
(default true) and passes `--no-default-features` when it is false, following
`rust.debug-logging` / `max_level_info`. The two are complementary:
`debug-logging` decides which `debug!`/`trace!` call sites are compiled,
`logging` decides whether anything is listening.

Measured on a stage1 `librustc_driver` for aarch64-apple-darwin, `strip -x`ed:
111,360,864 -> 110,703,864 bytes with `rust.logging = false`, -657,000. With
it left at the default the binary is unchanged (-8 bytes of build hash).

`x build compiler rustdoc clippy miri error_index_generator` and
`x check compiler` were run in both configurations.
